  "id": "ex-05-adjektivdeklination-b2",
  "intro": "Standalone drill set, not tied to any lesson. Closes out the Adjektivdeklination topic with two pieces: quantifiers before a Plural noun split into two groups — alle/beide act like a der-word, so the adjective after them takes the WEAK ending -en (alle guten Freunde); viele/einige/wenige/manche don't, so the adjective takes the STRONG ending -e in Nominativ/Akkusativ (viele gute Freunde, not viele guten Freunde) — and Partizip I (-end, \"the laughing man\") / Partizip II (\"the written letter\") used as adjectives, which decline exactly like any other adjective once formed. Blocks: A Basistraining → B Vertiefung → C Sprachbausteine → D Wiederholung — a full-topic mix. Answers in solutions.md.\n",
  "lesson": "EX/05-adjektivdeklination-b2",
  "level": "B2",
  "summary": null,
  "title": "Adjektive nach Quantoren & Partizipien als Adjektive — B2",
  "topic": "Adjektivdeklination (schwach, gemischt, stark)"
}
